SUMMARY:Deadline: Connect & Create: Live Performance and Music Circulation 
 2027 (Africa-Europe)
DESCRIPTION:Touring and circulation strand of Connect & Create\, the sub-Sa
 haran component of the EU-funded Africa-Europe Cultural Partnerships progr
 amme\, led here by the Institut francais and Expertise France in the Team 
 Europe spirit. It funds the circulation of African performing arts and mus
 ic creations in Africa and Europe. WHO CAN APPLY: artistic teams (performi
 ng arts companies\, musical ensembles\, collectives based in Africa)\, dis
 tribution structures (production offices\, artist development agencies\, s
 upport structures\, labels\, venues or cultural spaces in Africa or Europe
 ) and events (festivals\, markets\, trade shows or professional meetings i
 n Africa or Europe)\; structures must be based in sub-Saharan Africa or an
  EU country. PROJECT TYPES: tours in Africa with a minimum of 5 pre-booked
  dates in at least 3 countries outside the artist's country of residence\;
  tours in Europe with a minimum of 3 pre-booked dates\; or programming at 
 major events featuring at least 3 artistic teams from 3 different African 
 countries. PRIORITY goes to projects with originality and grounding in the
 ir context\, sustainable collaborations\, support for younger generations 
 and emerging scenes\, an eco-responsible approach\, and attention to inclu
 sion and accessibility. AMOUNTS: EUR 10\,000 to 20\,000 per project (EUR 1
 5\,000 to 25\,000 for delegations of 5+ nationalities)\, covering at most 
 70 percent of the budget\; at least 30 percent co-financing required. TIME
 LINE: projects run February to December 2027. APPLY via the Institut franc
 ais eMundus platform. Deadline 30 September 2026 at 23:59 Paris time.\n\nO
 rganisation: Institut francais and Expertise France\, with the Goethe-Inst
 itut (Africa-Europe Cultural Partnerships\, EU-funded)\nLocation: Tours an
 d events across sub-Saharan Africa and/or the European Union. Applicant st
 ructures must be based in sub-Saharan Africa or an EU country.\nAward: EUR
  10\,000 to 20\,000 per project\; EUR 15\,000 to 25\,000 for hosting inter
 national delegations representing at least 5 nationalities. Support is cap
 ped at 70 percent of the total project budget\, with at least 30 percent c
 o-financing (cash or in-kind) demonstrated by the applicant. Covers mobili
 ty costs: economy-class international\, national and local transport\, vis
 a fees and insurance\, accommodation and per diem\, and transport of sceno
 graphic and technical elements. No application fee.\nDuration: Projects mu
 st be carried out between February and December 2027\, in Africa\, Europe 
 or both. Deadline 30 September 2026 at 23:59 Paris time.\n\nMore: https://
 ifprog.emundus.fr/fr/campagne-info?view=programme&cid=353&utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ifprog.emundus.fr/fr/campagne-info?view=programme&cid=353&utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Tours and events across sub-Saharan Africa and/or the European Uni
 on. Applicant structures must be based in sub-Saharan Africa or an EU coun
 try.
