SUMMARY:Deadline: The Supporting Act Foundation: Impact Grant 2026 (10 x EU
 R 50\,000 for nonprofits)
DESCRIPTION:The Supporting Act Foundation's Impact Grant empowers arts-focu
 sed nonprofits that provide non-financial support to emerging artists from
  underrepresented groups\, aligned with TSAF's aims: improving artists' li
 ving conditions\, buying time for practice development\, increasing visibi
 lity\, and building confidence. AWARD: 10 unrestricted grants of EUR 25\,0
 00 per year over two years (EUR 50\,000 total per organization). ELIGIBILI
 TY: registered as a nonprofit arts organization between 2016 and 2024 in B
 elgium\, France\, Germany\, Greece\, Ireland\, Italy\, the Netherlands\, P
 ortugal\, Spain\, or the UK (nonprofits registered elsewhere may apply wit
 h a letter of intent from a fiscal host registered in one of those countri
 es)\; an IBAN bank account in the organization's or fiscal host's name\; t
 otal annual expenditure between EUR 50\,000 and 300\,000 in the current fi
 scal year\; and an updated website with public evidence of active projects
  providing non-financial support to underrepresented emerging artists. Not
  for individuals\, commercial organizations\, project proposals\, or curre
 nt or past TSAF grantees\; previously unsuccessful applicants may reapply.
  TIMELINE: call opens 1 September 2026\; review October\; notifications la
 te October\; final review of shortlisted applicants November\; announcemen
 t and first installment January 2027. DEADLINE: 1 October 2026\, 11:00AM C
 ET.\n\nOrganisation: The Supporting Act Foundation (TSAF)\nLocation: For n
 onprofit arts organizations registered in Belgium\, France\, Germany\, Gre
 ece\, Ireland\, Italy\, the Netherlands\, Portugal\, Spain\, or the UK\; n
 onprofits elsewhere may apply with a fiscal host registered in one of thos
 e countries.\nAward: 10 unrestricted grants of EUR 25\,000 per year over t
 wo years\, totalling EUR 50\,000 per organization. For nonprofits with ann
 ual expenditure between EUR 50\,000 and 300\,000. No application fee.\nDur
 ation: Two years\; public announcement and first installment January 2027.
 \n\nMore: https://thesupportingact.org/programs/impact-grant/2026?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
