SUMMARY:Deadline: SIM Residency: Funded Nordic-Baltic Residency\, January-F
 ebruary 2027 (Reykjavik)
DESCRIPTION:The SIM Residency in Reykjavik runs a funded January-February 2
 027 residency backed by the Nordic-Baltic Mobility Programme for Culture\,
  tailored for artists from the Nordic-Baltic region with a strong interest
  in sustainability\, ecology\, social equality and Nordic cultural narrati
 ves. Artists from diverse fields including visual arts\, performance\, sou
 nd\, digital media and research are encouraged to apply. SUPPORT: EUR 2\,0
 00 stipend for the whole period\, EUR 600 travel costs\, EUR 500 material 
 costs\, accommodation and studio facilities\, orientation\, artist present
 ation on SIM's website and social channels\, public presentation and artis
 t talk opportunities\, and studio visits with a curator\; participation in
  all program activities and the final exhibition is mandatory. ELIGIBILITY
 : four artists living in Denmark\, Finland\, the Faroe Islands\, Greenland
 \, Norway\, Sweden\, Aland\, Estonia\, Latvia or Lithuania (artists living
  in Iceland are excluded)\; a bachelor's degree in arts or equivalent prof
 essional experience is required. Apply via the online form with CV\, motiv
 ation letter\, 400-word project proposal\, up to 5 images and optional vid
 eo. Deadline: 1 October 2026.\n\nOrganisation: SIM Residency (Association 
 of Icelandic Visual Artists)\, funded by the Nordic-Baltic Mobility Progra
 mme for Culture\nLocation: Reykjavik\, Iceland\nAward: EUR 2\,000 stipend 
 for the whole period\, plus EUR 600 travel costs and EUR 500 material cost
 s\; accommodation and studio facilities included\nDuration: Two months\, 3
  January - 28 February 2027\; four artists selected\n\nMore: https://www.s
 im-residency.info/ncp-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
URL:https://www.sim-residency.info/ncp-2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Reykjavik\, Iceland
